blishes the new leader commitment boundary. Old election reply channels and old replication commitment objects remain separate from new attempts/terms. Latest logged configuration controls election and quorum membership before its commitment, but a further configuration requires prior configuration and current-term entry commitment. Conflicting follower suffix removal restores committed membership; snapshots restore configuration and applied prefix before suffix scanning or resumed participation. Already queued committed work remains FSM work across role change, while uncommitted leader futures become uncertain errors. VerifyLeader is a separate authority consumer using replication notifications; its voter-derived threshold and all-peer registration require eligibility investigation.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-membership\",\n        \"b-recovery\",\n        \"b-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-term\",\n        \"f-match\",\n        \"f-committed\",\n        \"f-verify-count\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-api-verify\",\n        \"s-append\",\n        \"s-commit\",\n        \"s-config\",\n        \"s-config-log\",\n        \"s-config-validate\",\n        \"s-dispatch\",\n        \"s-election-producer\",\n        \"s-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-install\",\n        \"s-leader-loop\",\n        \"s-lease\",\n        \"s-match\",\n        \"s-notify\",\n        \"s-repl-owners\",\n        \"s-replicate\",\n        \"s-start\",\n        \"s-verify\",\n        \"s-verify-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Transport-specific dispatch/order and cancellation contracts remain to be read before constructing schedules.\",\n      \"Storage partial failures and crash recovery atomicity remain unresolved.\",\n      \"Verification nonvoter eligibility is a sourced discrepancy, not an established violation.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both formation and